# Formatting Standards

Full examples: `skills/twincat3-code-style/references/formatting-rules.md` (Read when formatting or reviewing layout).

## Principles

| Topic | Rule |
|-------|------|
| Indent | 4 spaces, never tabs; continuation +4 from statement start |
| IF / FOR | `THEN` / `DO` on same line as keyword |
| ELSIF / ELSE / END_* | Column 0 |
| Single-line IF | Never — body always next line |
| CASE | Cases +4; multi-line body aligned; `ELSE` column 0 |
| STRUCT | `STRUCT` on own line after `:`; members +4; `END_STRUCT`/`END_TYPE` column 0 |
| Declarations | Align `:`, `:=`, `(* *)` within each VAR block |
| VAR order | INPUT → OUTPUT → IN_OUT → VAR → CONSTANT; group with `(* section *)` |
| Calls | ≤4 params one line; >4 multiline aligned `:=` / `=>` |
| Arrays | ≤30 elements one line; else multiline |
| Enums | ≤5 members one line; else one per line |
| Line length | Wrap at 200; wrap **after** binary operators |
| Assignments | Align `:=` in related groups |
| Blank lines | 1 before/after IF/CASE/FOR/WHILE; 0 between END_VAR and first stmt; max 1 consecutive |
| Spaces | Around operators and `:`; after commas; none before `.`/`[`/`(` |

Comments: `twincat3-comments.mdc` (only `(* *)`).
